43.351, 43.375, 43.398, 43.456, 43.491, 43.56, 43.63, 43.746, 43.804, 43.955, 44.129, 44.257]}, "quality_check": null, "script_sha256": "ab98b18548850500f50200463b00376340999fbcb95f3c3cf686c6650123f8a2", "text": "So they did. Liverpool became champions in 2020, with ninety-nine points. The breakthrough finally came. Remember that before dismissing everything Klopp said about City's finances as the bitterness of a man who couldn't win. He had won. He was on top. And he still thought financial rules mattered. That July, City successfully appealed their European ban at the Court of Arbitration for Sport. Most of the allegations were not established or were time-barred; a penalty remained for failing to cooperate. That was the UEFA case, separate from the later Premier League proceedings. Klopp was asked about it while Liverpool were already champions. Listen to what he chose to defend.", "voice_id": "bu5eKETbFKC8G702EAU4", "model_id": "eleven_multilingual_v2"}